  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Resolve a 2D Chamfer selection as closed loops plus joined open runs.\n- Keep each open run end to end. Enter and leave it on the air side.\n- Emit one edge-break record for each selected run.\n- Keep the existing cone, diameter, flute-length, wall, gouge, and stock checks.\n- Add the unattended design record for the open-run lead law.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Motion tests: `an_open_chamfer_rides_one_edge_from_end_to_end`, `connected_open_chamfer_edges_are_one_run`, and `separate_open_chamfer_chains_are_separate_passes`.\n- App tests: `a_selected_edge_generates_and_verifies_one_open_chamfer`, `connected_selected_edges_generate_one_open_pass`, `separate_selected_edges_generate_separate_open_passes`, and `an_open_chamfer_does_not_credit_an_unselected_edge`.\n- `cargo clippy -j 22 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` passed: 236 steps.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main` ran every reached motion and app lane. It reported 235 passed steps and one unrelated red step.\n- The red step is `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. It expected `(4716, 4688, 549)` and produced `(3158, 3130, 1141)`.\n- The same test failed with the same result after the issue diff was stashed on the `origin/main` baseline at `58cb641ca`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `graphify update` did not run because `graphify` is not on `PATH`.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer can now machine one or more selected open edge chains without cutting the complete edge loop.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2988\r\n",
